o that's what you need to do with your  business you need to decide you need to  decide that this is going to be  something important for you and you're  going to take action on it and when you  decide then the options open up the fear  goes away a little bit and you stay  focus on your task so decide  number two is create a schedule one of  the best ways that I know how to stay  focused on my task on my goal is to  create a schedule so this isn't your  full-time thing yet you have a certain  number of hours you dedicated to this  every week I would schedule that time in  that has to be really important time  right and this is for anybody who's  running the business or is doing it part  time you schedule in your CEO timer you  schedule in your task management time  and you don't allow interruptions right  you turn off your phone you know you  lock the door you don't check facebook  you know you don't watch youtube videos  even mine you're not watching my youtube  videos on these times and you sit down  and you work and you know you have this  amount of time every week or every day  to spend on your project and you get to  work so folks vote forces you it forces  you to stay focused on the time so look  at your schedule see how much time you  have and plot it out every week every  day however much time you have and don't  allow for any interruptions during that  time create a schedule number three is  launched quickly one of the hardest  thing to do as an entrepreneur is create  while you're in a vacuum you're creating  by yourself and there's nobody around  you to give you feedback to tell you  what to do to give you suggestions to  say hey what you're doing is great and  when you're just creating alone it can  be discouraging you don't know if you're  making progress or not you don't get the  feed off the energy of other people for  me it's hard to like I'm making these  videos I'm by myself and win a empty  room and I'm just talking to a camera  and what helps keep me going is knowing  that you guys are watching and and  you're leaving your comments and you're  giving me feedback and you're saying  Evan keep going you're saying these are  great videos that is fuel for me right  you need to get your fuel so you want to  launch your algorithms your software  whatever it is as soon as possible  there's a term in the software industry  called Minimum Viable Product where it's  basically don't spend all this time  creating the perfect product create  whatever is just enough that people will  use it because  you get their feedback you start to get  a little bit of market adoption of  people using it and they tell you why  it's good why it's bad we're to fix it  and that that's fuel because now you're  depending on other people right you're  you're providing the something that's  helping them out and that's fuel for you  to do better now you're not just by  yourself and when somebody writes to you  and says while your algorithms really  helped me with my project or my business  or whatever it is that makes you feel so  good that you'll want to keep going or  if somebody says hey I'd love it if your  algorithm could do this it gives you  something to work on and now you're you  have you almost have a boss you have  somebody that you're accountable to that  you have to get this done for and not  just yourself when your ideas and you'll  do it whenever so launch your product  launch your algorithms as quickly as  possible so you start getting feedback  and some fuel so in summary how to stay  focused number one decide number to  create a schedule number three launch  quickly and believe for those who are  watching you liked this video you can  subscribe to the channel you can support  me by clicking on the link in the  description and leave a comment let me  don't you think your comments mean a lot  to me and I love seeing them come in so  thank you so much I'll see you soon
 

